Meanwhile, Tzuyang had...

257
00:08:50,151 --> 00:08:52,060
- one more sponge cake.
- Of course.

258
00:08:52,061 --> 00:08:53,290
Eat slowly, please.

259
00:08:53,291 --> 00:08:55,161
(You make them compare us.)

260
00:08:55,991 --> 00:08:57,700
(This is how Tzuyang warms up.)

261
00:08:57,701 --> 00:08:58,960
- Then...
- Yes.

262
00:08:58,961 --> 00:09:01,030
- let's go to the first destination.
- Shall we get going?

263
00:09:01,031 --> 00:09:02,700
- Yes, shall we go?
- Shall we go now?

264
00:09:02,701 --> 00:09:03,701
Let's go.

265
00:09:03,702 --> 00:09:05,070
(Going to meet the first double of Mukho)

266
00:09:05,071 --> 00:09:06,470
- Tzuyang, - Yes.

267
00:09:06,471 --> 00:09:08,040
- do you have any siblings?
- I have one older brother.

268
00:09:08,041 --> 00:09:09,710
- You have an older brother, right.
- Yes.

269
00:09:09,711 --> 00:09:11,580
- I have an older brother.
- She looks like she has one.

270
00:09:11,581 --> 00:09:13,280
- Why?
- I just feel that.

271
00:09:13,281 --> 00:09:15,180
- How about me?
- I feel that too.

272
00:09:15,181 --> 00:09:16,280
- What about me?
- Really?

273
00:09:16,281 --> 00:09:17,451
Really?

274
00:09:17,781 --> 00:09:18,880
- Eun I...
- You...

275
00:09:18,881 --> 00:09:20,350
Eun I also looks like she has an older brother.

276
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,151
- You seem to have a younger sister.
- No.

277
00:09:22,551 --> 00:09:24,061
- I'm sorry.
- Only no younger sister.

278
00:09:24,261 --> 00:09:25,820
- She has an older brother.
- An older brother, an older sister,

279
00:09:25,821 --> 00:09:26,821
- And an older sister.
- and a younger brother,

280
00:09:26,822 --> 00:09:27,931
but no younger sister.

281
00:09:29,191 --> 00:09:30,700
How could I be so completely wrong?

282
00:09:30,701 --> 00:09:31,830
You amaze me.

283
00:09:31,831 --> 00:09:32,931
(Seon Min has awful intuition.)

284
00:09:33,161 --> 00:09:35,330
- Kyoung Pyo has an older sister.
- Yes.

285
00:09:35,331 --> 00:09:37,940
From behind, Kyoung Pyo looks like his sister.

286
00:09:37,941 --> 00:09:40,300
I do, right? I'm growing my hair.

287
00:09:40,301 --> 00:09:41,671
Why? Because of your role in a drama?

288
00:09:41,811 --> 00:09:43,411
- No, it's just my aesthetic.
- Just because?

289
00:09:43,671 --> 00:09:45,340
- Your aesthetic?
- What kind of aesthetic?

290
00:09:45,341 --> 00:09:47,211
If you mess up your aesthetic, you end up looking pathetic.

291
00:09:47,611 --> 00:09:49,880
I've looked pathetic for several times already.

292
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:51,081
(He's looked pathetic for several times already.)

293
00:09:51,281 --> 00:09:52,781
In the East Sea, there's a webfoot octopus that looks pathetic.

294
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:54,591
Is it true?

295
00:09:54,951 --> 00:09:56,350
You must be lying.

296
00:09:56,351 --> 00:09:57,390
I'm pretending I'm a professor...

297
00:09:57,391 --> 00:09:58,661
- of Marine and Fisheries.
- Sorry.

298
00:09:59,121 --> 00:10:00,891
I'm sorry that I didn't respond properly.

299
00:10:01,491 --> 00:10:03,231
Your humour styles don't match.

300
00:10:03,661 --> 00:10:05,530
- Let's get on the same page.
- Let's do that.

301
00:10:05,531 --> 00:10:07,371
It won't be easy. No chemistry, no fun.

302
00:10:08,231 --> 00:10:10,230
- No chemistry, no fun.
- I know people...

303
00:10:10,231 --> 00:10:11,941
who have chemistry with no fun.

304
00:10:12,271 --> 00:10:14,411
And there are people who are fun with no chemistry.

305
00:10:14,571 --> 00:10:16,311
But it's my first time seeing people with no chemistry and no fun.

306
00:10:17,511 --> 00:10:18,841
- We're in big trouble.
- No chemistry, no fun.

307
00:10:21,011 --> 00:10:23,080
So the hint started now, right?

308
00:10:23,081 --> 00:10:24,121
Yes, it did.

309
00:10:24,721 --> 00:10:26,880
How are the hints given?

310
00:10:26,881 --> 00:10:29,291
For example, on the street...

311
00:10:29,451 --> 00:10:30,451
So, look at him now.

312
00:10:30,721 --> 00:10:33,391
On the shirt of the jogger,

313
00:10:33,491 --> 00:10:35,760
- Right. Why is he jogging here?
- there could be a hint.

314
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:37,560
Right. It looks strange.

315
00:10:37,561 --> 00:10:38,600
Why is he running all of a sudden?

316
00:10:38,601 --> 00:10:40,260
It's strange. Why is he running here?

317
00:10:40,261 --> 00:10:41,830
His tattoo might be a fake.

318
00:10:41,831 --> 00:10:43,070
No, he looks...

319
00:10:43,071 --> 00:10:45,041
- He's a real runner.
- like he's running for real.

320
00:10:45,901 --> 00:10:49,441
(Is the jogger outside a B-Side?)

321
00:10:49,571 --> 00:10:51,040
- Excuse me, Tzuyang.
- Yes.

322
00:10:51,041 --> 00:10:52,511
We have a camera here, so you don't have to hold it.

323
00:10:52,741 --> 00:10:54,411
Is that so?

324
00:10:55,011 --> 00:10:56,050
- Goodness.
- She did it out of habit.

325
00:10:56,051 --> 00:10:57,281
Tzuyang did it out of habit.

326
00:10:57,681 --> 00:11:00,180
Since Tzuyang films her internet channel alone...

327
00:11:00,181 --> 00:11:02,091
It's an occupational hazard.

328
00:11:02,851 --> 00:11:05,061
Each has an occupational hazard.

329
00:11:05,491 --> 00:11:06,860
- Gosh, Tzuyang.
- You're so sharp.

330
00:11:06,861 --> 00:11:08,030
I didn't catch it.

331
00:11:08,031 --> 00:11:09,761
Tzuyang's hand was glued to the camera.

332
00:11:10,291 --> 00:11:11,460
The camera was fixed.

333
00:11:11,461 --> 00:11:14,471
(Ultimate professionalism)

334
00:11:15,731 --> 00:11:17,740
The sea and the sparkling water...

335
00:11:17,741 --> 00:11:19,601
- are so beautiful.
- So beautiful.

336
00:11:19,871 --> 00:11:22,441
- Isn't it so beautiful?
- Truly.

337
00:11:24,111 --> 00:11:27,241
(Mukho's ocean view makes them forget it all.)

338
00:11:28,611 --> 00:11:31,881
(Their ears are in paradise listening to the rolling waves.)

339
00:11:31,981 --> 00:11:33,951
There are so many raw fish restaurants here.

340
00:11:34,251 --> 00:11:36,751
- Right?
- Look at that.

341
00:11:36,991 --> 00:11:38,090
I think we're here.

342
00:11:38,091 --> 00:11:39,691
- Are we?
- Already?

343
00:11:39,761 --> 00:11:41,591
They have snow crab bread too.

344
00:11:41,691 --> 00:11:42,761
It must be good.

345
00:11:42,791 --> 00:11:44,531
- Thank you.
- Thank you for the ride.

346
00:11:46,661 --> 00:11:48,200
- Let's go.
- Hello.

347
00:11:48,201 --> 00:11:49,930
- It doesn't feel like I'm filming.
- This is so nice.

348
00:11:49,931 --> 00:11:51,470
- It feels like I'm on a trip.
- That's right.

349
00:11:51,471 --> 00:11:53,071
- It feels like a college retreat.
- It feels so good.

350
00:11:53,241 --> 00:11:54,941
It's like a college retreat.

351
00:11:55,111 --> 00:11:56,340
- Doesn't it?
- I'm so happy.

352
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:58,711
Don't say it in front of Jae Seok. He hasn't been to one.

353
00:11:58,981 --> 00:12:00,850
- I have.
- You haven't.

354
00:12:00,851 --> 00:12:02,011
- Is that true?
- I have.

355
00:12:03,251 --> 00:12:05,420
What? Is it this place?

356
00:12:05,421 --> 00:12:06,880
(Tangsuyuk)

357
00:12:06,881 --> 00:12:08,291
Is it here? A tangsuyuk place?

358
00:12:08,691 --> 00:12:10,351
- Is it here? They say it's here.
- Tangsuyuk?

359
00:12:11,521 --> 00:12:12,860
(First location: On-site reaction hint)

360
00:12:12,861 --> 00:12:14,230
(There's one more inside.)

361
00:12:14,231 --> 00:12:17,291
(It fits perfectly.)

362
00:12:17,501 --> 00:12:19,960
They were frying tangsuyuk.

363
00:12:19,961 --> 00:12:20,970
(The sizzling sound was frying tangsuyuk.)

364
00:12:20,971 --> 00:12:22,500
It was a sizzling sound.

365
00:12:22,501 --> 00:12:24,941
- But how come they covered this?
- That's strange.

366
00:12:25,401 --> 00:12:28,111
(The restaurant is completely covered with blinds.)

367
00:12:28,311 --> 00:12:30,770
It looks so suspicious. Is this really a tangsuyuk place?

368
00:12:30,771 --> 00:12:31,781
I know.

369
00:12:32,341 --> 00:12:34,380
The sign looks so easy to make.

370
00:12:34,381 --> 00:12:35,381
(The sign looks so easy to make.)

371
00:12:35,951 --> 00:12:37,821
You can make something like that in a minute.

372
00:12:38,721 --> 00:12:39,881
Hanging it would take a minute.

373
00:12:41,921 --> 00:12:44,561
- The tangsuyuk smell is strong.
- I can definitely smell it.

374
00:12:44,761 --> 00:12:45,891
There's a strong smell of fried food.

375
00:12:46,191 --> 00:12:48,731
- But I can feel fish too.
- Yes.

376
00:12:48,961 --> 00:12:49,961
And tangsuyuk...

377
00:12:49,962 --> 00:12:52,701
How come a tangsuyuk place has such high ceilings?

378
00:12:53,701 --> 00:12:57,431
(A tangsuyuk place with a fishy smell and high ceilings?)

379
00:12:58,201 --> 00:13:00,100
(What's the first double in Mukho they will encounter here?)

380
00:13:00,101 --> 00:13:01,241
For now, have a seat, please.

381
00:13:02,311 --> 00:13:04,280
It smells so good, though.

382
00:13:04,281 --> 00:13:05,880
- I like the scent.
- Isn't it, dude?

383
00:13:05,881 --> 00:13:07,980
- It is.
- Seon Min...

384
00:13:07,981 --> 00:13:10,310
It's so real that I can't even imagine it being fake.

385
00:13:10,311 --> 00:13:12,820
This place can't be fake.

386
00:13:12,821 --> 00:13:15,091
- There's nothing strange here.
- Shall we bring the owner?

387
00:13:15,191 --> 00:13:16,751
- Excuse me.
- By the way,

388
00:13:16,891 --> 00:13:18,220
the balloon flower root I had earlier keeps repeating on me.

389
00:13:18,221 --> 00:13:19,591
(He had a balloon flower root latte earlier.)

390
00:13:19,921 --> 00:13:22,461
(The fatal presence of the balloon flower root)

391
00:13:23,531 --> 00:13:25,901
It tasted too strong.

392
00:13:26,101 --> 00:13:27,901
- Gosh, I can feel it in my neck.
- Hello.

393
00:13:28,001 --> 00:13:29,371
- Hello.
- Hello.

394
00:13:29,571 --> 00:13:31,471
(The owner appears right on time.)

395
00:13:31,841 --> 00:13:33,241
Seon Min...

396
00:13:33,301 --> 00:13:34,411
On this side...

397
00:13:34,611 --> 00:13:35,670
They have a similar vibe.

398
00:13:35,671 --> 00:13:37,211
They look similar.

399
00:13:38,241 --> 00:13:40,541
I thought Seon Min was coming.

400
00:13:40,581 --> 00:13:41,811
Sir, in this restaurant,

401
00:13:42,081 --> 00:13:44,520
what is double? We have no idea.

402
00:13:44,521 --> 00:13:47,081
Our tangsuyuk is not ordinary.

403
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:50,590
Octopus is tightly stuck to the pork loin.

404
00:13:50,591 --> 00:13:51,660
- What?
- It's made that way...

405
00:13:51,661 --> 00:13:52,661
What?

406
00:13:53,121 --> 00:13:54,690
- At our restaurant...
- Pork and octopus are stuck...

407
00:13:54,691 --> 00:13:56,630
- together on tangsuyuk?
- That's right.

408
00:13:56,631 --> 00:13:58,661
- They're served together?
- Pork and octopus...

409
00:13:59,161 --> 00:14:00,361
Really?

410
00:14:00,661 --> 00:14:02,630
Octopus and pork are not separated, but served together?

411
00:14:02,631 --> 00:14:03,971
Yes, they're put together.

412
00:14:04,771 --> 00:14:06,801
(Can it be true?)

413
00:14:07,341 --> 00:14:09,471
You can eat pork and octopus in one bite.

414
00:14:10,311 --> 00:14:13,211
I'm Kim Ji Woong, the owner of this octopus tangsuyuk place.

415
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:17,351
I thought about what kind of business I should run here.

416
00:14:17,551 --> 00:14:19,021
I decided to start the business with this unique tangsuyuk...

417
00:14:19,781 --> 00:14:24,461
that fits the East Sea.

418
00:14:24,861 --> 00:14:28,331
I tried seafood like squid,

419
00:14:28,591 --> 00:14:31,931
and mixed vegetables too.

420
00:14:32,301 --> 00:14:35,001
But the octopus went well with pork and tasted good.

421
00:14:35,671 --> 00:14:38,701
So I fried octopus and pork together.

422
00:14:39,171 --> 00:14:42,271
First, I started at a 6.6m² container in Jungang Market.

423
00:14:42,941 --> 00:14:46,140
Now I'm running a business in a 132m² space.

424
00:14:46,141 --> 00:14:47,181
(Customers like the double menu, so he runs a spacious shop.)

425
00:14:47,441 --> 00:14:49,450
On weekends or busy hours,

426
00:14:49,451 --> 00:14:52,021
there's a waitlist of 50 to 60 groups.

427
00:14:52,821 --> 00:14:57,351
(Mukho's definitive signature restaurant)

428
00:14:57,761 --> 00:15:00,661
(The double menu that attracts Mukho visitors)

429
00:15:00,961 --> 00:15:04,731
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

430
00:15:07,601 --> 00:15:09,201
(I see.)

431
00:15:09,371 --> 00:15:11,241
- The storyline fits perfectly.
- May I ask...

432
00:15:11,541 --> 00:15:12,941
if you're originally from here?

433
00:15:13,001 --> 00:15:15,310
My hometown is Geoje Island.

434
00:15:15,311 --> 00:15:16,910
- You're from Geoje.
- Geoje?

435
00:15:16,911 --> 00:15:18,580
- You're from Geoje.
- Geoje?

436
00:15:18,581 --> 00:15:20,341
- We...
- Geoje?

437
00:15:20,511 --> 00:15:22,451
Geoje, yaho!

438
00:15:23,781 --> 00:15:25,351
(Laughing)

439
00:15:28,151 --> 00:15:29,550
It just feels so stuffy.

440
00:15:29,551 --> 00:15:30,821
(Seon Min's version feels rather stuffy.)

441
00:15:31,421 --> 00:15:32,720
I will do it as much as I can.

442
00:15:32,721 --> 00:15:34,121
- Yaho.
- Geoje, yaho.

443
00:15:34,661 --> 00:15:35,961
Yaho!

444
00:15:36,091 --> 00:15:37,561
(Addictive)

445
00:15:37,731 --> 00:15:39,901
Is it the only menu here, or do you have other dishes?

446
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,800
Our place is known for tangsuyuk with octopus and pork.

447
00:15:42,801 --> 00:15:46,301
You can have jumbo jjajangmyeon with octopus...

448
00:15:46,801 --> 00:15:48,371
to enjoy with tangsuyuk.

449
00:15:49,071 --> 00:15:50,671
Jjajangmyeon.

450
00:15:52,941 --> 00:15:54,210
You digested...

451
00:15:54,211 --> 00:15:55,511
- the balloon flower root, right?
- I love it.

452
00:15:55,851 --> 00:15:57,150
The balloon flower root is going down quickly.

453
00:15:57,151 --> 00:15:58,721
I need to wash down the balloon flower root.

454
00:15:59,921 --> 00:16:01,420
- Bring it quickly, please.
- The balloon flower root...

455
00:16:01,421 --> 00:16:03,221
is bubbling in my stomach.

456
00:16:03,491 --> 00:16:05,361
(He's so funny.)

457
00:16:05,591 --> 00:16:07,990
I'm very excited today.

458
00:16:07,991 --> 00:16:09,030
- I see.
- Yes.

459
00:16:09,031 --> 00:16:11,031
- I'll cook it right away.
- Thank you.

460
00:16:11,761 --> 00:16:13,361
Jumbo jjajangmyeon,

461
00:16:13,961 --> 00:16:15,471
- I'll definitely eat you up.
- It's crazy.

462
00:16:16,471 --> 00:16:20,041
BIBI, after the Waterbomb is over...

463
00:16:21,111 --> 00:16:23,011
Has your inner foodie taken over?

464
00:16:23,411 --> 00:16:26,380
Almost. She ate the fish-shaped crackers last night.

465
00:16:26,381 --> 00:16:27,441
She's going wild.

466
00:16:27,911 --> 00:16:30,180
But after a week,

467
00:16:30,181 --> 00:16:31,750
- Is there another show?
- it's a Waterbomb again.

468
00:16:31,751 --> 00:16:32,751
Oh, my.

469
00:16:33,081 --> 00:16:34,591
It's just until today.

470
00:16:34,691 --> 00:16:35,920
- You will eat.
- I'm eating...

471
00:16:35,921 --> 00:16:39,590
and starting a diet tomorrow. I will control my appetite tomorrow.

472
00:16:39,591 --> 00:16:41,590
You don't say that you're not going to eat.

473
00:16:41,591 --> 00:16:42,891
(That's what I'm saying.)

474
00:16:43,131 --> 00:16:44,961
If I don't eat, I get a terrible attitude.

475
00:16:45,461 --> 00:16:47,201
I know some people are like that.

476
00:16:47,431 --> 00:16:50,331
Tzuyang, are there any symptoms that show when you're hungry?

477
00:16:50,701 --> 00:16:53,801
I rarely make myself hungry.

478
00:16:54,611 --> 00:16:56,111
(I see.)

479
00:16:56,311 --> 00:16:57,711
(Beyond imagination)

480
00:16:58,011 --> 00:16:59,040
You never stop eating.

481
00:16:59,041 --> 00:17:00,381
- She's wise.
- She doesn't let herself starve.

482
00:17:00,781 --> 00:17:03,081
I rarely let my stomach go empty.

483
00:17:03,181 --> 00:17:06,050
If that ever happens,

484
00:17:06,051 --> 00:17:08,591
I literally can't do anything.

485
00:17:08,691 --> 00:17:11,491
- Really?
- I just lose all my energy.

486
00:17:12,191 --> 00:17:14,021
Is the interval between your meals about two hours?

487
00:17:14,291 --> 00:17:16,261
No, I just keep eating.

488
00:17:16,531 --> 00:17:17,591
No, I mean...

489
00:17:18,431 --> 00:17:21,231
(I shouldn't have asked that.)

490
00:17:21,601 --> 00:17:23,071
She's on a different level.

491
00:17:23,671 --> 00:17:26,800
What surprised me was that she ate 10m of beef small intestines.

492
00:17:26,801 --> 00:17:28,540
Right.

493
00:17:28,541 --> 00:17:29,870
It was 16m.

494
00:17:29,871 --> 00:17:30,971
- It's 16.
- Is it 16?

495
00:17:31,641 --> 00:17:33,040
(16m of beef small intestines?)

496
00:17:33,041 --> 00:17:34,180
- Then...
- A single cow produces 16m...

497
00:17:34,181 --> 00:17:36,151
of beef small intestines.

498
00:17:36,251 --> 00:17:37,680
- From a single cow.
- If it's 16m,

499
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:40,051
it would be enough for a group jump rope.

500
00:17:40,121 --> 00:17:41,820
You can do group jump rope with 16m of those.

501
00:17:41,821 --> 00:17:43,521
It's unbelievable.

502
00:17:44,591 --> 00:17:46,361
You basically cleared out the entire inside of a cow.

503
00:17:46,421 --> 00:17:49,091
I keep getting goosebumps.

504
00:17:49,191 --> 00:17:51,201
You ate 16m of it?

505
00:17:51,401 --> 00:17:52,530
You eat a lot indeed.

506
00:17:52,531 --> 00:17:54,330
The smell of frying is already...

507
00:17:54,331 --> 00:17:55,901
- It smells good.
- Totally.

508
00:17:56,031 --> 00:17:58,140
I must really be hungry right now.

509
00:17:58,141 --> 00:18:00,041
