00:46:19,001 --> 00:46:23,571
I thought adding seafood would make it taste better.

1278
00:46:24,511 --> 00:46:26,710
Koreans add noodles or sujebi...

1279
00:46:26,711 --> 00:46:29,441
to their soup dishes.

1280
00:46:29,581 --> 00:46:32,081
In China, it's common to add knife-cut noodles.

1281
00:46:33,451 --> 00:46:35,721
(Knife-cut noodles are commercialized too.)

1282
00:46:35,851 --> 00:46:38,391
I added it to gamjatang, and it was chewy and nice.

1283
00:46:38,791 --> 00:46:41,121
So I imported the machine from China...

1284
00:46:41,221 --> 00:46:43,361
and completed the gamjatang we're selling now.

1285
00:46:44,691 --> 00:46:47,461
(Doubled-up gamjatang! How does it taste?)

1286
00:46:48,001 --> 00:46:49,671
(That's novel.)

1287
00:46:49,901 --> 00:46:53,201
Did you run a restaurant back in China too?

1288
00:46:53,571 --> 00:46:54,640
No.

1289
00:46:54,641 --> 00:46:56,140
No, he didn't run a restaurant in China.

1290
00:46:56,141 --> 00:46:57,671
How did you think to open one in Korea?

1291
00:46:58,141 --> 00:47:01,241
I learned from my father-in-law after I got married.

1292
00:47:02,211 --> 00:47:05,680
My father-in-law is at Jungang Market.

1293
00:47:05,681 --> 00:47:07,120
- Jungang Market.
- There's Jungang Market nearby...

1294
00:47:07,121 --> 00:47:08,121
That's right.

1295
00:47:08,451 --> 00:47:10,920
After he got married.

1296
00:47:10,921 --> 00:47:12,121
(He started the restaurant with his in-law's help.)

1297
00:47:12,321 --> 00:47:15,120
I'm so curious. Could we try it?

1298
00:47:15,121 --> 00:47:17,131
Yes, sure.

1299
00:47:17,991 --> 00:47:20,461
(Glancing)

1300
00:47:20,801 --> 00:47:22,931
Perhaps the owner is a Mandarin teacher.

1301
00:47:24,501 --> 00:47:27,971
Isn't he too real to be a Mandarin teacher?

1302
00:47:28,571 --> 00:47:32,271
He's wearing a gold necklace. Chinese like gold.

1303
00:47:32,371 --> 00:47:33,641
I'm sure Seon Min likes gold too.

1304
00:47:34,481 --> 00:47:35,640
(You bet.)

1305
00:47:35,641 --> 00:47:38,411
I really like it too, actually.

1306
00:47:39,821 --> 00:47:42,050
(Is the Chinese owner with the gold necklace real?)

1307
00:47:42,051 --> 00:47:44,520
He can show you the performance too.

1308
00:47:44,521 --> 00:47:45,750
- He prepared it.
- Yes.

1309
00:47:45,751 --> 00:47:47,190
- I'm curious.
- Would you like to see it?

1310
00:47:47,191 --> 00:47:48,260
- Yes.
- I'm curious.

1311
00:47:48,261 --> 00:47:49,860
I'm curious to see how it will cut.

1312
00:47:49,861 --> 00:47:51,161
(Heony's knife-cut noodles performance)

1313
00:47:51,991 --> 00:47:54,400
(Pour enough amount of flour.)

1314
00:47:54,401 --> 00:47:55,800
You pour it in advance...

1315
00:47:55,801 --> 00:47:57,371
- so the noodles don't stick.
- In advance.

1316
00:47:58,001 --> 00:47:59,601
- That's...
- The dough.

1317
00:48:00,041 --> 00:48:03,840
You need to let the dough rest first.

1318
00:48:03,841 --> 00:48:04,841
(He takes out the rested dough.)

1319
00:48:05,111 --> 00:48:06,941
Where does the dough go?

1320
00:48:07,681 --> 00:48:10,111
- The head?
- The head?

1321
00:48:10,981 --> 00:48:13,121
(The dough goes...)

1322
00:48:13,921 --> 00:48:15,450
- Not the head.
- There?

1323
00:48:15,451 --> 00:48:16,991
So you place it there and cut it.

1324
00:48:17,451 --> 00:48:18,990
- It works?
- Does it work?

1325
00:48:18,991 --> 00:48:20,260
Since it's knife-cut noodles,

1326
00:48:20,261 --> 00:48:21,760
you don't pull it out from the machine.

1327
00:48:21,761 --> 00:48:23,130
You cut it like that.

1328
00:48:23,131 --> 00:48:24,291
(He's like the 2nd owner.)

1329
00:48:25,031 --> 00:48:28,261
(Press the "start" button.)

1330
00:48:30,131 --> 00:48:31,930
(Heony's right hand...)

1331
00:48:31,931 --> 00:48:34,271
(moves flashily.)

1332
00:48:36,941 --> 00:48:38,670
(At its firm movement,)

1333
00:48:38,671 --> 00:48:41,441
(the noodles bid farewell without lingering.)

1334
00:48:42,211 --> 00:48:45,281
(Cutting skills from overseas)

1335
00:48:45,851 --> 00:48:48,851
(Heony's cutting show opens.)

1336
00:48:49,381 --> 00:48:51,690
- It slowly goes down.
- It's so quick.

1337
00:48:51,691 --> 00:48:55,220
That's it. Here it goes.

1338
00:48:55,221 --> 00:48:57,830
Here it goes.

1339
00:48:57,831 --> 00:48:59,261
It's splashing a lot.

1340
00:49:00,761 --> 00:49:01,901
It's splashing a lot.

1341
00:49:02,301 --> 00:49:03,670
- My gosh, it...
- It...

1342
00:49:03,671 --> 00:49:04,731
(Adjusting the basin)

1343
00:49:05,101 --> 00:49:06,870
Technology has improved so much.

1344
00:49:06,871 --> 00:49:08,141
I know, right?

1345
00:49:08,871 --> 00:49:11,110
You would've needed a master for it before.

1346
00:49:11,111 --> 00:49:12,511
(Quite a lot of noodles have been collected already.)

1347
00:49:13,381 --> 00:49:15,941
(Once there's enough, turn off the power.)

1348
00:49:16,551 --> 00:49:18,211
- Noodles.
- My eyes...

1349
00:49:18,611 --> 00:49:20,151
Can you show us?

1350
00:49:22,451 --> 00:49:23,690
Look.

1351
00:49:23,691 --> 00:49:26,790
(Knife-cut noodles made by Heony)

1352
00:49:26,791 --> 00:49:27,821
It looks delicious.

1353
00:49:28,591 --> 00:49:29,730
Even in that state?

1354
00:49:29,731 --> 00:49:31,790
- I couldn't see it with my eyes.
- I...

1355
00:49:31,791 --> 00:49:33,400
- It cut so fast.
- I can see its future.

1356
00:49:33,401 --> 00:49:35,031
(I can see the noodles' future.)

1357
00:49:35,061 --> 00:49:36,500
They'll serve us food now, right?

1358
00:49:36,501 --> 00:49:39,201
- If this place is fake...
- This is...

1359
00:49:40,401 --> 00:49:42,300
- We'll serve the side dishes first.
- Okay.

1360
00:49:42,301 --> 00:49:43,570
(The side dishes are served first.)

1361
00:49:43,571 --> 00:49:45,741
- It looks good.
- Take kimchi.

1362
00:49:46,071 --> 00:49:47,541
There's one radish kimchi too.

1363
00:49:48,241 --> 00:49:50,780
This... Tzuyang, you already got it.

1364
00:49:50,781 --> 00:49:52,351
(She takes radish kimchi first.)

1365
00:49:52,451 --> 00:49:55,680
(Cutting)

1366
00:49:55,681 --> 00:49:57,150
- You're so good.
- Am I?

1367
00:49:57,151 --> 00:49:58,591
Since I eat so much.

1368
00:49:59,421 --> 00:50:01,321
She's super fast only when it comes to eating.

1369
00:50:02,491 --> 00:50:04,491
- Tzuyang...
- That's right.

1370
00:50:04,791 --> 00:50:07,030
has become lively after eating.

1371
00:50:07,031 --> 00:50:09,260
I can't speak on an empty stomach.

1372
00:50:09,261 --> 00:50:10,901
- You couldn't.
- Right.

1373
00:50:11,001 --> 00:50:12,570
I thought you were angry during the opening.

1374
00:50:12,571 --> 00:50:13,601
(Teasing)

1375
00:50:14,041 --> 00:50:15,070
I'm sorry.

1376
00:50:15,071 --> 00:50:16,471
(I wasn't angry. I was hungry.)

1377
00:50:18,311 --> 00:50:19,910
Yes, please bring it.

1378
00:50:19,911 --> 00:50:21,140
It's huge.

1379
00:50:21,141 --> 00:50:22,280
(What's that?)

1380
00:50:22,281 --> 00:50:23,281
What's that?

1381
00:50:23,511 --> 00:50:25,080
(The ultimate...)

1382
00:50:25,081 --> 00:50:26,720
(triad...)

1383
00:50:26,721 --> 00:50:28,051
(is here.)

1384
00:50:28,321 --> 00:50:30,350
- Yes, please bring it.
- It's huge.

1385
00:50:30,351 --> 00:50:32,250
(Gamjatang with seafood and knife-cut noodles is here.)

1386
00:50:32,251 --> 00:50:33,860
- What's this?
- This...

1387
00:50:33,861 --> 00:50:35,591
(Shocked by its visual)

1388
00:50:36,761 --> 00:50:38,331
(It's not a freeze frame.)

1389
00:50:38,961 --> 00:50:40,700
(Only here,)

1390
00:50:40,701 --> 00:50:43,000
(you can try this menu.)

1391
00:50:43,001 --> 00:50:45,970
Add pork backbone, water, and soju into a big pot...

1392
00:50:45,971 --> 00:50:47,271
and boil for ten minutes.

1393
00:50:48,901 --> 00:50:50,240
Add grilled vegetables and the special sauce...

1394
00:50:50,241 --> 00:50:51,541
to give it the unique taste of my restaurant.

1395
00:50:54,041 --> 00:50:55,581
Boil it well for 40 minutes.

1396
00:50:57,451 --> 00:50:59,651
(Delicious-looking gamjatang base is complete.)

1397
00:51:00,081 --> 00:51:05,151
Add potatoes and dried radish greens and boil for five more minutes.

1398
00:51:06,621 --> 00:51:08,790
Add the seafood, mushrooms, water parsley, and so on...

1399
00:51:08,791 --> 00:51:11,961
every five minutes...

1400
00:51:12,861 --> 00:51:14,231
and wait until they're cooked.

1401
00:51:16,001 --> 00:51:18,200
(Pile up the chunks in the pot first.)

1402
00:51:18,201 --> 00:51:21,141
Pour the soup and cooked knife-cut noodles.

1403
00:51:23,411 --> 00:51:25,711
(Gamjatang with seafood and knife-cut noodles)

1404
00:51:26,241 --> 00:51:28,881
(It went viral on social media for the machine-cut noodles.)

1405
00:51:29,341 --> 00:51:32,351
(It became a famous spot in Mukho that you need to queue up.)

1406
00:51:32,711 --> 00:51:35,721
The monthly sales is about 90,000 to 100,000 dollars.

1407
00:51:36,351 --> 00:51:39,991
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

1408
00:51:41,861 --> 00:51:44,160
- I can't tell if it's real or fake.
- Amazing.

1409
00:51:44,161 --> 00:51:46,501
The portion is huge.

1410
00:51:46,801 --> 00:51:48,130
How many servings is this?

1411
00:51:48,131 --> 00:51:49,431
This is a big size.

1412
00:51:50,071 --> 00:51:52,131
Normally, a big size is for four people.

1413
00:51:52,431 --> 00:51:53,770
- Four to five.
- This is a lot.

1414
00:51:53,771 --> 00:51:55,170
But the ingredients...

1415
00:51:55,171 --> 00:51:56,271
(Okay, size checked.)

1416
00:51:56,441 --> 00:51:59,071
Tzuyang is getting ready by drinking.

1417
00:52:00,011 --> 00:52:01,440
Is she opening her throat?

1418
00:52:01,441 --> 00:52:02,941
(Waking up her oesophagus)

1419
00:52:03,511 --> 00:52:07,581
(If you're ready, let's eat!)

1420
00:52:07,981 --> 00:52:09,720
Noodles first.

1421
00:52:09,721 --> 00:52:11,020
- Noodles first.
- Noodles first.

1422
00:52:11,021 --> 00:52:12,421
Next, seafood.

1423
00:52:13,221 --> 00:52:14,460
Noodles, seafood,

1424
00:52:14,461 --> 00:52:15,490
- and...
- Noodles first.

1425
00:52:15,491 --> 00:52:16,931
- Because noodles become soggy.
- Noodles first.

1426
00:52:17,691 --> 00:52:20,530
- Shall we try the noodles first?
- Yes.

1427
00:52:20,531 --> 00:52:21,731
Noodles first.

1428
00:52:22,301 --> 00:52:25,371
(Dip knife-cut noodles in the soup.)

1429
00:52:26,071 --> 00:52:27,270
(Jae Seok takes a big bite.)

1430
00:52:27,271 --> 00:52:28,671
- Goodness.
- The noodles...

1431
00:52:29,841 --> 00:52:33,071
(The small eater eats one strand.)

1432
00:52:34,141 --> 00:52:35,940
(BIBI drinks from the bowl.)

1433
00:52:35,941 --> 00:52:37,681
This tastes like my grandma's dish.

1434
00:52:38,511 --> 00:52:40,381
(I agree.)

1435
00:52:40,851 --> 00:52:45,020
(Tzuyang takes a big bite too.)

1436
00:52:45,021 --> 00:52:46,860
Rather than knife-cut noodles,

1437
00:52:46,861 --> 00:52:48,820
doesn't it taste more like handmade kalguksu?

1438
00:52:48,821 --> 00:52:50,730
- The noodles are interesting.
- They are.

1439
00:52:50,731 --> 00:52:52,031
It's a bit like kaljebi too.

1440
00:52:52,561 --> 00:52:55,360
Gosh, this gamjatang...

1441
00:52:55,361 --> 00:52:57,170
(The kaljebi-like texture makes it fun to chew.)

1442
00:52:57,171 --> 00:52:58,730
This is right up my alley.

1443
00:52:58,731 --> 00:53:00,070
(This is right up my alley.)

1444
00:53:00,071 --> 00:53:02,300
I thought the taste would be complicated.

1445
00:53:02,301 --> 00:53:04,110
I thought it would taste complicated,

1446
00:53:04,111 --> 00:53:05,141
but it's clear.

1447
00:53:05,471 --> 00:53:06,941
It has a clear message.

1448
00:53:08,041 --> 00:53:11,011
Sixty percent of seafood is added compared to an ordinary gamjatang.

1449
00:53:12,681 --> 00:53:14,920
You taste both seafood and gamjatang.

1450
00:53:14,921 --> 00:53:16,150
(Seafood and gamjatang taste at the same time)

1451
00:53:16,151 --> 00:53:18,720
The crab meat has flaked apart,

1452
00:53:18,721 --> 00:53:20,291
so it tastes a bit like crab and kimchi stew too.

1453
00:53:21,821 --> 00:53:23,090
I love crab and kimchi stew.

1454
00:53:23,091 --> 00:53:24,830
(While everyone is enjoying eating, Seon Min is looking for something.)

1455
00:53:24,831 --> 00:53:26,360
You need a bigger bowl.

1456
00:53:26,361 --> 00:53:28,731
It's okay. I'll use the small one.

1457
00:53:30,701 --> 00:53:32,201
I want to change to a small one.

1458
00:53:35,441 --> 00:53:37,011
They gave me such a big bowl.

1459
00:53:37,271 --> 00:53:39,271
- Just eat.
- Okay.

1460
00:53:39,911 --> 00:53:41,810
I thought it'd taste lighter...

1461
00:53:41,811 --> 00:53:43,550
because of the seafood,

1462
00:53:43,551 --> 00:53:45,050
- but it's very heavy.
- It's heavy.

1463
00:53:45,051 --> 00:53:47,120
I think it's because of the pork backbone.

1464
00:53:47,121 --> 00:53:50,120
I think so too. The whole backbone is inside.

1465
00:53:50,121 --> 00:53:51,821
(It keeps its identity as gamjatang thanks to the backbone.)

1466
00:53:52,921 --> 00:53:56,491
(Eating backbone)

1467
00:53:57,431 --> 00:54:01,531
(Tzuyang, on another level, uses her hand.)

1468
00:54:01,901 --> 00:54:04,330
- It's smoky.
- It sure does.

1469
00:54:04,331 --> 00:54:05,470
Like...

1470
00:54:05,471 --> 00:54:08,900
- the smoked flavour of sausages.
- Yes, the smoked flavour.

1471
00:54:08,901 --> 00:54:09,970
- Right?
- I taste it.

1472
00:54:09,971 --> 00:54:11,210
Why does it taste smoky?

1473
00:54:11,211 --> 00:54:12,370
(Because it's boiled with grilled vegetables,)

1474
00:54:12,371 --> 00:54:14,981
(the meat is tender and has a smoky flavour.)

1475
00:54:15,681 --> 00:54:17,511
(Eun I takes a bite too.)

1476
00:54:17,711 --> 00:54:19,151
- It's good.
- It's good.

1477
00:54:19,781 --> 00:54:22,081
(Everyone is clearing their bowl.)

1478
00:54:22,521 --> 00:54:24,450
(Jae Seok eats it straight off the bone.)

1479
00:54:24,451 --> 00:54:25,551
I got fooled.

1480
00:54:26,591 --> 00:54:27,891
I thought it was meat, but it's a bone.

1481
00:54:30,131 --> 00:54:32,291
- Watch out for your teeth.
- Are you okay?

1482
00:54:32,761 --> 00:54:34,331
My teeth are fine!

1483
00:54:35,261 --> 00:54:36,700
BIBI said,

1484
00:54:36,701 --> 00:54:38,171
"Watch out for your teeth."

1485
00:54:38,801 --> 00:54:41,740
Just in case it straightens your teeth.

1486
00:54:41,741 --> 00:54:43,740
He'll be in trouble if they straighten.

1487
00:54:43,741 --> 00:54:46,170
You could have the national MC position taken away.

1488
00:54:46,171 --> 00:54:47,611
If my crooked teeth...

1489
00:54:48,011 --> 00:54:49,940
become straight by accident?

1490
00:54:49,941 --> 00:54:51,251
Yes. Just in case.

1491
00:54:51,551 --> 00:54:53,851
(Just thinking about it makes her laugh.)

1492
00:54:54,851 --> 00:54:56,650
(Glancing)

1493
00:54:56,651 --> 00:54:58,790
Kyoung Pyo, shall we give them some since we have a lot?

1494
00:54:58,791 --> 00:55:00,691
We should. I'll do it.

1495
00:55:00,891 --> 00:55:01,920
Shrimps and all.

1496
00:55:01,921 --> 00:55:03,830
(He spots that.)

1497
00:55:03,831 --> 00:55:05,591
Two of you clearly look like...

1498
00:55:06,031 --> 00:55:09,601
a director who came for trading...

1499
00:55:10,731 --> 00:55:12,230
- A site visit.
- Yes.

1500
00:55:12,231 --> 00:55:14,241
A manager and a director who are here for a site visit.

1501
00:55:14,741 --> 00:55:16,601
This table's vibe is...

1502
00:55:17,341 --> 00:55:18,810
Assuming we're of similar ages,

1503
00:55:18,811 --> 00:55:20,541
it's a failed group blind date.

1504
00:55:22,081 --> 00:55:24,350
- This table...
- It's a very tense vibe.

1505
00:55:24,351 --> 00:55:25,850
Someone arranged this blind date for them.

1506
00:55:25,851 --> 00:55:28,350
They came with high expectations,

1507
00:55:28,351 --> 00:55:29,850
- but they're done.
- They're done.

1508
00:55:29,851 --> 00:55:31,291
Their weekend is ruined.

1509
00:55:31,521 --> 00:55:33,220
- Now...
- They're just focusing on the food.

1510
00:55:33,221 --> 00:55:36,320
The guys are like, "I know a nice pasta place."

1511
00:55:36,321 --> 00:55:38,331
But the girls go, "Let's just eat gamjatang."

1512
00:55:40,101 --> 00:55:42,001
I intuitively figured it out.

1513
00:55:42,331 --> 00:55:44,231
But he's still clueless.

1514
00:55:44,601 --> 00:55:46,231
Eat up. What would you like?

1515
00:55:46,431 --> 00:55:47,740
- Should I peel the shrimps for you?
- He's still...

1516
00:55:47,741 --> 00:55:49,641
No thanks, I'll help myself.

1517
00:55:50,341 --> 00:55:52,570
- I...
- He keeps talking to one...

1518
00:55:52,571 --> 00:55:54,041
- I'll help myself.
- of the two.

1519
00:55:54,341 --> 00:55:56,040
Tzuyang doesn't even bother to respond.

1520
00:55:56,041 --> 00:55:58,150
She's just eating.

1521
00:55:58,151 --> 00:55:59,151
Isn't it delicious?

1522
00:55:59,381 --> 00:56:00,921
(Nodding)

1523
00:56:00,951 --> 00:56:02,080
It's delicious.

1524
00:56:02,081 --> 00:56:03,280
(The situation is so funny.)

1525
00:56:03,281 --> 00:56:05,890
I'm actually in a situationship with someone else,

1526
00:56:05,891 --> 00:56:07,761
so I'm not interested either.

1527
00:56:08,561 --> 00:56:09,561
- What?
- Seon Min...

1528
00:56:09,562 --> 00:56:10,761
No.

